Let a memory have four free blocks of sizes $\text{4k, 8k, 20k, 2k}$. These blocks are allocated following the first-fit strategy. The allocation requests are stored in a queue as shown below from multiple processes executing concurrently.
$$\begin{array}{|l|c|c|c|c|c|c|c|c|c|}\hline \textbf{Request No.} & \text{$T_1$} & \text{$T_2$} & \text{$T_3$} & \text{$T_4$} & \text{$T_5$} & \text{$T_6$} & \text{$T_7$} & \text{$T_8$}
\\\hline
\textbf{Request Sizes} & \text{2k}& \text{14k}& \text{3k}& \text{6k}& \text{6k} & \text{10k}& \text{7k}& \text{20k}
\\\hline
\textbf{Usage Time} & \text{4} & \text{10} & \text{2}& \text{8}& \text{4}& \text{1}& \text{8} & \text{6}
\\\hline\end{array}$$
The time at which the request for $T_6$ will be completed will be ________

$X$ is a random variable that follows a continuous uniform distribution with probability density function
$$f(x) = \left\{\begin{matrix}
\dfrac{1}{9} &;2012\leq x \leq 2021 \\
0 &;\text{otherwise}
\end{matrix}\right.$$
If the $\alpha$ is the expectation, and $\beta$ is the variance of the distribution, then the value of $\alpha - \beta$ is ________ (upto two decimal places)
